# Bounded session autonomy

Activate with `/autonomy` or when the user explicitly starts a bounded autonomy campaign.

## Rules

1. Prefer parallel `Task` launches for independent read/fix slices (one message for all ready work).
2. If waiting on PR CI/reviews: **spawn a background poll subagent** (`Task` + `run_in_background: true`); **main continues** other work.
3. Never block the main turn on CI when a poll worker can own that PR (no `AwaitShell` / `gh pr checks --watch` on a PR that has an active poll worker).
4. Never autonomous merge — report merge-gate eligibility; wait for explicit human approval.
5. Skill composition: one primary (`l9-bounded-autonomy`) + ≤2 supporting; do not auto-invoke explicit-only skills.
6. Campaign authority is a **campaign authorization packet** (not an “envelope”).
7. Deep contracts: `skills/l9-bounded-autonomy/` and Claude runtime under `environment/agents/adapters/claude-code/autonomy/` (do not rewrite the Python scheduler from Cursor).
